Coaches can split one session time(slot) btwn multiple students
*Design (added 2026-10-12): skaters per lesson in the schedule editor; client book-share-*.html, invite*.html, bookings-shared.html, home-invited.html; coach pending, day and payments pages; rinkside today-shared*.html.*


~~Q: how many students max are allowed to split a lesson. 
Let the coach decide this? or hard code?~~ *Answered: default 1, max 2 (ADR-026 P1).*


The owner's answers after talking with an end user (2026-10-06):
  Every booking starts private. A family books a time as today and it shows as taken. Other families never see that
    a time could be shared, or how many skaters it holds.
  Sharing is by invitation. While booking, the family can add another family's skater. That family confirms, and
    then the booking shows both.
  The coach decides how many skaters each block allows.
  *(from ADR-026 Context, moved 2026-11-08)*

Decided 2026-10-07:

Coach: when the coach makes the schedule they set how many skaters can split each lesson (per block).
  Default value is 1 (private). Default max is 2. The max might be raised later.

Client booking:
  The client does not see how many skaters can share a lesson.
  A "share this lesson" box only shows on times whose block allows 2 or more.
  Only 1 skater code can be entered in the box.
  Note in the box: skater 2's family must accept before skater 2 can join the lesson.
  On entering a skater code, the system checks the skater exists and shows first name and last initial (e.g. Mia R.).
  The booking only continues once skater 2 is validated as existing.
  A code that doesn't check out stops the booking at that step. Families can tell a time is shareable, never how
    many skaters it takes. Family A's lesson is then booked as normal, private.
    *(from ADR-026 §5 "On the booking screen", moved 2026-11-08)*
  Share code: every skater has one (e.g. MIA-4K7QX), shown on their profile in the family website. A family gives it
    to the family they want to share with, the same way a coach gives out their coach code. It never changes
    (owner, 2026-10-13; see ClientProfileView). *(from ADR-026 §4 and Status, moved 2026-11-08)*
  *Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033 d2, d2a): the code must also belong to a skater the coach has accepted (ACTIVE). As soon
    as the code is entered, the booking page asks the share-check endpoint. If skater 2 isn't the coach's student, the
    booking stops at the share step with: "Mia R. isn't one of Coach Dana's students yet. Mia's family can sign up with
    Coach Dana's code, and once Coach Dana accepts Mia you can share a lesson." Nothing is booked. The booking itself
    checks again in the database, so a skater declined in between is still refused.
    Book stays off while the share-code box has anything in it, until the check passes. If the check fails or is rate-limited: "Couldn't check that code. Try again." Changing the code checks again; clearing it books a private lesson. (ADR-033 2a, 2026-10-20)*
  *ADR-033 2a (owner, 2026-10-20), in full:* Book stays disabled while the share-code box has anything in it, until the
    share-check for that exact code and coach says the skater is on the coach's roster. That covers a code still being
    typed, a check in flight, a code that doesn't exist, the skater's own code, a skater not on the roster, and a
    failed or rate-limited check ("Couldn't check that code. Try again."). Changing the code, or the picks' coach,
    clears the answer and checks again. Clearing the box allows a private booking. This is a screen rule only; the
    booking itself checks again. *(from ADR-033 decision 2a, moved 2026-11-08)*

Coach acceptance:
  A student must always be accepted by the coach before any lessons are booked for that student.
  ~~A client can invite a skater the coach hasn't accepted, but nothing is booked for skater 2 until the coach accepts them.~~
  ~~If the coach does not accept skater 2 (or doesn't act before the lesson), the lesson proceeds as a private lesson.~~
  *Changed 2026-10-20:* Only a skater the coach has accepted can be invited or added as a sibling (ADR-033).
  *Added 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 5): skater 2's place is held from the moment the lesson is booked, so no other
  family can take it while they're invited~~ or waiting for the coach~~. Skater 2 pays nothing until they join. If they
  never join, the lesson stays private at the full price.*

Invitation (changed 2026-10-07):
  When a family splits a lesson, an email is sent to family B straight away.
  *Decided by the owner 2026-10-13 (ADR-025 item l):* shared-lesson invitations name their coach on every family page
    (home banner, invitations card, invitation page). The invitation emails already did.
    *(from ADR-025, amendment 2026-10-13, item l, moved 2026-11-08; also in ClientHomeView, "Across coaches")*
  If skater B is already the coach's student, the email is a normal invite to accept or decline.
  ~~If skater B is not part of that coach, the email says something like:~~
    ~~"Coach XXX needs to accept you first. By clicking the link below you agree to be added to Coach XXX's roster of students."~~
  ~~The link opens a confirmation page.~~ Family B must sign in and confirm on the page.
  The confirmation page shows skater B any conflicting bookings they would have. They can go ahead or cancel.
  ~~If they go ahead, the request follows the same flow as if they had entered the coach code at sign up.~~
  ~~When the coach accepts skater B, skater B joins the lesson automatically.~~
  *Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033): the email is always a normal invite to accept or decline; inviting a skater new to the
    coach, and the consent link, are Phase 2. Family B's own accept joins the lesson.*
  Before writing anything, the job checks that the lesson slot still exists and hasn't happened yet.
    *Per ADR-026 d5: ~~done by the coach's Accept itself, which also checks~~ ~~there's room and~~ ~~that the booking named this skater.~~*
  If those aren't true it does nothing, and family B is notified that the booking didn't happen.
    *Changed 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 6): the place is already held, so there is always room. The Accept only checks
    that the lesson is still there and hasn't started.*
    *Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033 d3): the check is made by family B's own accept, after confirming skater B is still the
    coach's student; the coach's Accept no longer touches lessons. If skater B is no longer the coach's student, family B
    sees "no longer available".*
  *Phase 2 record (ADR-026 d5, 2026-10-07; Phase 2 since ADR-033, 2026-10-20):* when skater B isn't the coach's
    student, the email says, in substance: "Coach Dana needs to accept you first. By following the link below you
    agree to be added to Coach Dana's roster of students, and Mia will join the lesson on Tue 14 Oct at 4:00 once
    Coach Dana accepts." An earlier version of the 2026-10-07 decision had the coach see only a display name and the
    invited family hear nothing until the coach accepted; the owner replaced it the same day with the consent link.
    The 2026-10-07 flow in short: the share box shows only on shareable times and takes one code; booking waits for
    the code to check out; the invited family is emailed straight away; a skater new to the coach joins the coach's
    roster through a consent link; the invited family confirms on a signed-in page that shows any clashes; once the
    coach accepts, the skater joins if the lesson still exists, hasn't happened and has room, and otherwise the
    invited family is told; one invitation covers a whole series; a sibling is added directly.
    *(from ADR-026 Status amendment 2026-10-07 and §5 step 2, moved 2026-11-08)*
  Recurring booking: the code shares every lesson in the series.
    *Added 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 6): a series joins lesson by lesson. Each date succeeds or fails on its own, and
    family B gets the dates that work.*
  Sibling (same family): just booked, no confirmation needed ~~(still needs coach acceptance first)~~.
  *Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033): only a sibling the coach has already accepted can be added. A sibling not yet accepted
    shows as "not available to add until Coach Dana accepts them" and can't be picked.*
    *(from ADR-033 decision 2, moved 2026-11-08)*
  Designs revisited (ADR-033 Consequences): the Harbor screens for inviting a skater new to the coach
    (design/harbor/client/static/invite-new-student.html and the demos), the warning banners, and the coach's pending
    list showing shared-lesson context. Done 2026-10-20: those pages are removed, and book-share-not-student,
    book-share-sibling-waiting and invite-accepted show the new behaviour. *(from ADR-033 Consequences, moved 2026-11-08)*
  *Added 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 12):* ~~the "not yet accepted" warning is sent at the 9pm run before it's due, so
    it's never late and never sent at night.~~ Expiry when the lesson starts is checked every hour, and its email goes
    at once.
  *Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033 d5): there is no "not yet accepted" warning; it is Phase 2 with the consent link.*

See docs/adr/ADR-026-shared-lessons-by-invitation.md.



Decided 2026-10-13 (owner; ADR-026 amendment, ADR-015 amendment):

Price:
  The lesson has one set price, the schedule's price for that block. When shared it is split between the skaters:
  a $50 lesson for two skaters is $25 each. Until the second skater joins, the booking family pays the full price.
  Personal prices are Phase 2, so the split is always of the schedule's price.
  The invitation page and My bookings show each family their own share.
  *Added 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 7):*
    The price is split evenly between the skaters who have joined. An invited skater~~, or one waiting for the coach,~~
      pays nothing yet.
    Odd cents go one each to the skaters who joined first (owner: "I don't care which"). $45.01 for two is $22.51
      and $22.50.
    *Owner, 2026-11-11 (B10):* every page works a share out as the price divided by the number of skaters splitting
      it, never as "half". The booking pop-up says "Once they join, the lesson's $50 is split between the skaters:
      with 2 skaters, each pays $25." The invitation page says "$25 for Zoe: the lesson's $50, split between 2 skaters."
    Shares are worked out again whenever who's paying changes: a skater joins, a freed place is filled, the staying
      family keeps a lesson at the full price, or the coach changes the price.
    ~~A lesson already marked paid or waived never changes.~~ *Revised 2026-10-13 (ADR-031): its price follows the
    lesson time; a lesson paid in advance and then re-priced isn't handled (ADR-031 Revisit if).*
    *Revised 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 revision, decision 7): a share isn't stored. Only the lesson's total price is kept,
      with the number of skaters splitting it, and each share is worked out from those. ~~A skater's amount is fixed
      only when they're checked in, marked a no-show, or marked paid or waived. After that it never changes, even if
      the coach changes the price.~~ Nothing on one family's lesson changes because of the other family.*
    *Revised 2026-10-13: no amount is copied onto a seat; it's worked out from the lesson time (ADR-031 d7).*

A skater calls out (either family; the booking family is not a special case):
  In time (before the coach's notice period): the other family is told and chooses to keep the lesson as a private
    lesson at the full price, or cancel with no charge. ~~No answer by the start of the notice period cancels it,
    with no charge.~~ (home-share-left.html, bookings-cancel-shared.html)
    *Changed 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 8): they answer by whichever comes first, the start of the notice period or
    7 days after the other skater left. Nothing waits for more than a week. No answer by then cancels it with no
    charge; this is checked every hour. Their share stays as it was until they answer.*
    *Revised 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 revision, decision 8): the question is recorded on the lesson, not on the staying
    family's booking. Their booking isn't changed until they answer.*
    *Open:* whether the 7 days in the answer-by rule should be a question for Kim. *(Put to Kim as §8 Q7.)*
    *(from ADR-031 Open, moved 2026-11-08)*
  Late (inside the notice period) or a no-show: the one who called out may be charged
    their share of the late-cancellation fee (half, for two skaters).
    The other skater keeps their share.
    The skater who stays isn't charged any fee. *(from ADR-026 Status amendment 2026-10-13, moved 2026-11-08)*
  No special case for the booking family (P4): once both skaters have joined, either family leaving follows the same
    rules. The invited family can cancel from My bookings like the booking family.
    *(from ADR-026 Status amendment 2026-10-13, moved 2026-11-08)*
  *Added 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 5, option B):* ~~If the inviting family cancels before the other skater has joined, the invitation ends: at once if it wasn't answered yet, or within the hour (the invited family is emailed) if they'd accepted.~~ Withdrawing is only possible before the other family answers.
  *Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033 d4):* If the inviting family cancels while the invitation is still unanswered, it ends at
    once. If the invited family has already accepted, the cancel is an ordinary leave, in time or late (ADR-033 d4).

*Added 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decisions 9 and 10):*
A shared repeating lesson:
  While a series is shared, a family can only cancel one lesson or cancel the series. "End it earlier" and "Make it
    less frequent" are hidden. A series counts as shared while any future lesson in it has another skater, joined or
    invited. Once none does, both choices come back.
  The same answer-by rule applies whether the other skater cancels one lesson or the whole series.
  When the other skater leaves several dates, the staying family gets one card for the series, with Keep all
    remaining dates, Cancel all remaining dates, and a choice per date (see cancelation.md).

A freed place:
  When the staying family keeps a lesson at the full price, that lesson becomes a freed place.
  "Invite a skater" appears on it in My bookings. This is the only place sharing is offered after booking.
  It works like sharing while booking: the new skater's place is held at once, the staying family pays the full
    price until the new skater joins, then the price is split.
  It covers that one lesson only, never a series.
  The new skater goes through the same steps: their family accepts~~, the coach approves them if they're new~~, they join.
    *Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033): the new skater must already be the coach's student.*
  Filling a freed date in a series makes the series shared again until that lesson is over.

Coaches see every skater (ADR-026 decision 6, 2026-10-06):
  The coach's week view, lesson list, payments and the rinkside page show every skater in a shared time, each with
    their own attendance and payment status.
  A coach cancelling a lesson, day or week cancels every skater in it, and each family is told.
  *(from ADR-026 §6, moved 2026-11-08)*

Screens this feature needs (ADR-026 Consequences, 2026-10-06): the share code on a skater's profile; "add a skater to
  share" on booking; invitations to confirm or decline; both skaters on a shared booking; every skater in a time on
  the coach's views. None was in the Harbor designs then. *2026-10-13: designed in design/harbor (family and coach
  sites).* *(from ADR-026 Consequences, moved 2026-11-08)*

Rejected: open spots any family can book, with the remaining count shown. Rejected by the owner: every booking is
  private until the booking family chooses to share. *(from ADR-026 Alternatives considered, moved 2026-11-08)*

Phase 2: an invitation waiting on the coach (decided by the owner 2026-10-09; Phase 2 since ADR-033, 2026-10-20):
  This only applies to a skater new to the coach, which is Phase 2. In MVP an invitation unanswered when the lesson
    starts expires with the ordinary "no longer available" email.
  The warning: for each lesson whose invitation is still waiting on the coach, an email goes to both families and the
    coach no later than 24 hours plus the coach's notice period before the lesson. Families who have opted in to
    texts also get a text pointing to the email. The coach's email was moved from Phase 2 to MVP by the owner
    (2026-10-09), before ADR-033 moved the whole warning to Phase 2.
    To both families: "Coach Dana hasn't accepted Mia for the shared lesson on Tue 14 Oct at 4:00. If she doesn't,
      the lesson goes ahead as a private lesson."
    To the coach: a shared lesson on Tue 14 Oct at 4:00 is waiting for you to accept Mia, with a link to the pending
      list.
    The timing gives family A at least a day before the notice period begins, so they can cancel without a late fee
      if they don't want a private lesson.
  The banner: from the warning time until the coach accepts or declines skater B, or the lesson starts, both
    families' home screens show a red banner.
    Family A: "Coach Dana hasn't confirmed Mia for your shared lesson on Tue 14 Oct at 4:00. Unless she does, it will
      go ahead as a private lesson, charged at the booking's own price."
    Family B: "Coach Dana hasn't accepted Mia yet. If she doesn't before the lesson, Mia won't join the Tue 14 Oct
      4:00 lesson."
    "The booking's own price" is what family A booked at, so the banner stays true whatever was decided about shared
      pricing. *2026-10-13: decided; until a second skater joins, the lesson is private at the full price.*
  Family B's email when the lesson expires and the coach never accepted skater B: "This lesson has expired. Please
    reach out to Coach Dana to be accepted onto her roster for any future shared lessons. Reply to this email to
    reach Coach Dana."
  *(from ADR-026 Status amendment 2026-10-09 and §5a, moved 2026-11-08)*

Questions P1–P5 (were for Kim; all answered by the owner. None of them blocked private booking):
  P1. The most skaters a coach may allow in one lesson. Answered 2026-10-07: 2, as a setting that may be raised.
  P2. How a shared lesson is priced. Answered 2026-10-13: the lesson's set price is split between the skaters; a
    skater leaving in time leaves the other family to choose full price or cancel; leaving late, the other keeps
    their share.
  P3. Must an invited skater already be approved by this coach? Answered 2026-10-07: no to be invited; yes before
    any lesson is booked for them. Kim §6 can't remove this approval. *Superseded for MVP 2026-10-20 by ADR-033: the
    skater must already be the coach's student to be invited.*
  P4. If the booking family cancels, what happens to the invited skaters? Answered 2026-10-13: the same as either
    skater leaving.
  P5. If an invitation isn't confirmed in time? Partly answered 2026-10-07: if the coach hasn't accepted the skater,
    the lesson goes ahead private. Answered 2026-10-13: an invitation the family hasn't accepted has no cutoff before
    the lesson; it expires when the lesson starts, and the lesson goes ahead private. ~~Leaning towards the coach's
    notice period (24 hours by default)~~
  *(from ADR-026 "Pending Kim", moved 2026-11-08)*
